<?xml version="1.0"?>
<page xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
      xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:View/Layout/etc/page_configuration.xsd">
    <body>
        <!--
            Renderer one: the card template.

            `product_list_item` is the block Hyvä renders every card through — see
            `Hyva\Theme\ViewModel\ProductListItem::getItemHtml()`, which looks the block up by that
            exact name. Repointing its template is the whole integration: category listings, search
            results, the compare page and Hyvä's own product slider all reach the card through this
            one block, so none of them needs its own hook.

            It is also, honestly, a fork of Hyvä's `product/list/item.phtml`. The template it
            replaces reproduces Hyvä's structure deliberately (same form, same child blocks, same
            order) so third-party injections keep working, and the README says what to re-check
            after a Hyvä upgrade.

            **This instruction alone does not take effect, and is kept as the statement of intent.**
            Hyvä declares `product_list_item` in the *theme*, and
            `View\Layout\File\Collector\Aggregated::getFiles()` collects every module file before it
            loops over the inherited themes — so the theme's declaration is merged last and puts its
            own template back, without an error anywhere. `Observer\ApplyCardTemplate` re-applies
            the template on `layout_generate_blocks_after`, which is what actually makes the card
            render. To go back to the stock card, switch the module off in configuration
            (`scr1be_product_card/general/enabled`); the observer checks it first. The ViewModel
            layer, the GraphQL fields and the minicart plugins are unaffected either way.
        -->
        <referenceBlock name="product_list_item" template="Scr1be_HyvaProductCard::product/list/card.phtml"/>
    </body>
</page>
